-- title:
--   Restriction of the Hopf kernel to an idempotent sub-part
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $A$ be a commutative ring which is a Hopf algebra over $K$, finite as a $K$-module and with cocommutative comultiplication, and let $\bar A$ be a commutative ring which is a Hopf algebra over $K$. Let $\pi : A \to \bar A$ be a surjective $K$-bialgebra map. Here, for a bialgebra map $\rho : A \to B$, $\mathrm{hopfKer}\,\rho$ denotes the $K$-subalgebra of $A$ on which the algebra map $(\mathrm{id}_A \otimes \rho) \circ \Delta_A$ agrees with $a \mapsto a \otimes 1$. Assume given an idempotent $e \in A$ with $\Delta(e)\,(e \otimes 1) = e \otimes e$ and $\varepsilon(e) = 1$, and an idempotent $f \in \mathrm{hopfKer}\,\pi$ with $f e = e$ and such that every $b \in \mathrm{hopfKer}\,\pi$ with $b e = 0$ satisfies $b f = 0$. Assume further given commutative Hopf $K$-algebras $A_f$ and $\bar A_f$ together with surjective $K$-bialgebra maps $\pi_f : A \to A_f$ and $\pi'_f : \bar A \to \bar A_f$ whose kernels, as maps of $K$-algebras, are the ideals generated by $1 - e$ and by $1 - \pi(e)$ respectively, and a $K$-bialgebra map $\pi_{ff} : A_f \to \bar A_f$ with $\pi_{ff}(\pi_f(x)) = \pi'_f(\pi(x))$ for all $x \in A$. Then the image of the subalgebra $\mathrm{hopfKer}\,\pi$ under $\pi_f$ equals $\mathrm{hopfKer}\,\pi_{ff}$.
--
--   In the dual language of finite commutative group schemes over a field of characteristic $0$, with $V = \operatorname{Spec} A$ having geometric points on which $\pi$ cuts out a subgroup $W$, $e$ the indicator function of a subgroup $E$ and $f$ that of $EW$, this is the function-algebra form of the second isomorphism theorem $E/(E \cap W) \cong EW/W$: the $W$-invariant functions on $EW$ restrict onto the $(E \cap W)$-invariant functions on $E$. It is used by [`HopfAlgebra.map_hopfKer_eq_hopfKer_of_finitePartIdempotent`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.map_hopfKer_eq_hopfKer_of_finitePartIdempotent), where the minimal idempotent $f$ above is produced from the data of the quotient.
